er you want the universe the order  of providence  punishes us from making these wrong  decisions so that's our fault too  and augustine says that doesn't really  cut it for me  because who made me that way in the  first place  and you know if we do this in sort of a  traditional uh  christian cosmology you know you can  sort of  push things back and say well you know  the devil  puts bad suggestions in people's minds  and then they follow along with them and  how'd that guy go wrong how that angel  will run  sooner or later sooner or later  you have to push the problem back to  god and say look you're going to say  that god is all-powerful  all-knowing you know he says all all  everything  existence itself supreme existence so  why is there evil this is a big problem  so augustine is going to offer us an  account  of how not to address this  problem and get a satisfactory answer  he says i thought to myself  just imagine everything imagine the  totality of  all created being all that is trees  mountains you know we'd imagine cell  phones and bookshelves and  subways and roads and  skies and pick whatever you like you  know we have a much uh  better you know knowledge of the  universe than  augustine himself did so just imagine  the entire cosmos right  and where this tiny little speck in the  middle of it that doesn't matter  imagine all that now bring it before  your mind is  one gigantic totality  augustine says god is greater than that  so god is kind of like something  you know transcending that  so not all of being not all of the  existence  is in the universe as a matter of fact  created being he says  is kind of like a sponge uh you know  it's full of holes  and god sort of penetrates everywhere so  it's like a super super sponge  um and later on he will say this isn't  the right way to conceive of god but  this is the way that he's understanding  god at that time  so this brings up a big problem  where the hell does evil come from  can it come in from the outside remember  god's supposed to be totally good  god's creating everything  god you know interpenetrates everything  so there's really no  outside for evil to come in  because there isn't an outside beyond  created being  and the transcendent god who somehow  encompasses it  that's it that's that's the totality of  of reality there isn't anything  there's no multiverse because if there  was a multiverse that would be inside  here  so this isn't going to work  it's too bad because that would provide  an explanation for  where evil comes from and then augustine  says  that's a big problem you know why  does that mean that evil is actually  nothing  but wait a second we experience evil we  fear evil  or maybe is here's a really interesting  suggestion that he makes  is that fear itself the origin of evil  is that how everything got started  but you know that that he doesn't  actually you know trace this out that  really wouldn't work because  fear of what fear of  of evil of something that's bad of  something that's that's  destroying corrupting uh perverting  something that is opposed to what  what is good what is you know what ought  to be so  keep these in the back your mind for a  moment now he explores some other  possibilities he says  well we know that there's evil  right we're fine with that  we're not going to say that it just sort  of popped out of nothing  because you know nothing comes from  nothing it's not  just popping out of our fear because  what is our fear of in order to make  that happen  maybe it's god's fault still  so god through his creative activity  created everything that is  but what had he created out of well you  know  another way of getting around this  problem of attributing evil to god  would be to say that you know  god created  everything  are actually not everything out  of some sort of evil  stuff will not even necessarily call it  matter  anything you like could be ideas  could be energy could be whatever you  like  augustine is using you know the term  matter here  because he's thinking in terms of you  know traditional ancient cosmologies  and in terms of of the gnostics who he's  you know targeting  um mainly under the manikin form  but you could you could pick whatever  you like yet the basic idea would be  that god doesn't  actually create from nothing god has to  have something to work with  and there's something wrong with that  stuff  there's some primal original fault sin  blame evil defect  in the stuff and he can't make it do  what it ought to do or be what it ought  to be  and so evil creeps into the world  through  created existence  does that really resolve the problems  well it depends on your conception of  god  let's say for a moment that we're not  assuming that god created everything out  of nothing  that there is some sort of stuff that  god actually creates  from some primal material  that he uses that he comes across  the primal materials got some sort of  problem with it  why didn't he make it better if he's  omnipotent  if he's omniscient if he's all good why  didn't he take that  original goop or latticework or pick  whatever you like  and fix it wouldn't that have been a  more reasonable thing to do  that's what augustine you know suggests  here  so this is not actually going to get us  out of the  the problem um he says  he would not be omnipotent where he ate  not able to create something good  without being assisted by that matter  which had not been created by himself  he says so i went round and round  thinking about this sort of stuff  and i never really arrived at a  satisfactory conclusion this is why  we're talking about this is getting evil  wrong  god creates everything out of nothing so  this isn't going to work  so where does evil come from we go back  to the original point  which is that evil arrives  within being is a kind of  nothing that is parasitical upon  something namely the plentitude of good  created being and it does so through  certain types of beings that is  beings that actually have a free will  that's going to be augustine's solution  to this that he arrives at in the very  end of  of the confessions where he began is  where he ends he doesn't provide us with  a full  discussion of that that's going to come  in other core concept videos this one  was primarily just about  what were ways to not get this get this  right  the origin of evil and so we've covered  those  they were evil comes in from the outside  because there isn't any outside for it  to come in out of  evil comes about because god has crappy  materials to begin with and isn't able  to actually make them work  that's not going to work either either  evil comes about  because of our fear of evil well that  presupposes that there's already evil  there  so those are not going to work within a  traditional theistic  framework you could say well then just  abandon the traditional theistic  framework that's not what this video is  about this video is more  about looking at these these ways of not  properly conceptualizing the problem of  evil

